From 54af025ad590fcc63a08b9cc6c3f99e4a5ed8320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bernhard=20Rosenkr=C3=A4nzer?= <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:43:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posix: Do not double-free regex arrays when allocation fails
 (CVE-2026-100290)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

re_dfa_add_node and build_range_exp grew several arrays and stored the
new pointers only after every realloc had succeeded.  When a later
realloc moves a block it frees the old one, and the error path freed
that pointer again.  match_ctx_add_entry freed bkref_ents on realloc
failure while leaving the pointer for match_ctx_free.

Store each successful realloc before returning, and on failure leave
the new block in place.  Do not free it and do not clear the pointer
realloc left valid.

check_arrival points state_log at path->array.  An error return left
both pointers to be freed, including after extend_buffers replaced the
array.  Restore the caller's state_log on every exit from that window.
check_matching must report an allocation failure as -2.  Returning
REG_ESPACE made the caller treat error 12 as a match index.
A NULL state-log entry at a reported match is REG_ESPACE, not a halt
state to dereference.

Upstream published GLIBC-SA-2026-0028 with no Fix-Commit.

Reported-by: Tristan <TristanInSec@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
---
 NEWS                              |   4 +
 posix/Makefile                    |   1 +
 posix/regcomp.c                   |  32 +++--
 posix/regex_internal.c            |  27 ++--
 posix/regexec.c                   |  45 ++++---
 posix/tst-regcomp-alloc-failure.c | 207 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 273 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 posix/tst-regcomp-alloc-failure.c

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index e5a223b4..738612c8 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ Version 2.44.1
   the initial shift state already stores the terminating NUL
   (CVE-2026-115819, GLIBC-SA-2026-0027).
 
+* regcomp and regexec no longer free the same allocation twice when
+  growing an internal array fails (CVE-2026-100290,
+  GLIBC-SA-2026-0028).
+
 The following bugs are resolved with this release:
 
   [33085] libc: nftw: readdir() errors are ignored
